Article 2 (Establishment and Functions)
A Committee for Comprehensive Social Reform (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") shall be established under the Prime Minister to provide advice to the Prime Minister concerning the following matters relating to political, economic, social and cultural reforms (hereinafter referred to as "comprehensive social reform"):
1. Realization of democracy and social justice;
2. Establishment of peaceful cooperation between South and North Korea and pragmatic diplomacy;
3. Educational reform;
4. Protection of socially vulnerable persons;
5. Economic justice and stability of the people's livelihoods;
6. Responses to the climate crisis, realization of an ecological society, and securing food sovereignty;
7. Balanced regional development;
8. Other matters for comprehensive social reform that the Prime Minister deems necessary to refer to the Committee for advice or that the Chairperson of the Committee deems necessary.
